Copyright (c) 2026 Rafael C. R. de Lima. All rights reserved.

This repository is private. The Daedalus source code is not distributed and no
licence is granted to use, copy, modify, distribute or host the code, nor the
visual identity files.

What is free is the PROGRAM. Anyone may use Daedalus, for any purpose, at no
cost and without signing up, wherever it is published — in class, in research,
in a paper. The networks, simulations, exported files and figures you produce
with it are yours. Using the program grants no licence over its code.

The code Daedalus EMITS — the C++, Wolfram Language and Python files produced
by the exporters — is yours, to compile, run, modify and publish as you wish,
including as supplementary material to a paper. This release covers the
generated file as a whole, including the numerical core embedded in it.

For anything else — bundling Daedalus into another project, publishing a copy,
deriving a version — ask the author for permission.

A technical note, not a legal one: Daedalus runs entirely in the browser, so
the published JavaScript and WebAssembly are readable by anyone who opens the
developer tools. This notice is about permission, not secrecy.
